course: dictionary
lesson: 10878
title: Words for places and people
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A village is a small group of houses and people in the country, smaller than a town. «Farmers built houses of mud brick or wood near their fields and lived in villages all year round.» The houses sit near the fields, so the words around village tell you it is a place in the countryside.
explain: The word can also mean all the people who live there. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about buildings and land, or about people?
explain: Context can also show a figure of speech. In «a global village», the word is not about houses at all. It means the whole world feels close because people can talk across it. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word: does it still make sense?
fact: A village is smaller than a town.
fact: «Villages» is the plural of village.
fact: In everyday life, a village may have a few shops, a church or a school, a green or a pub, and everyone knows everyone.
fact: In history and geography, villages can grow into towns and cities.
fact: «Global village» means the whole world feels close because people can talk across it.
exercise: «Farmers built houses of mud brick or wood near their fields and lived in villages all year round.» What is a village? | A very large city full of tall buildings | A road between two fields | *A small group of houses and people in the country | A kind of farm animal
exercise: Which is bigger than a village? | A small green | A single house | *A town | A farm gate
exercise: Ruby reads «a global village» and says it means a small place in the country. What does it really mean? | *The whole world feels close because people can talk across it | A group of farmers who grow wool | A village that has grown into a city | A small place with a green and a pub
test: In «Mei's grandmother was sent to a village as a girl», what does village mean? | *A small group of houses and people in the country | A river with a stone bridge | A kind of tree | A type of hero
test: Which sentence uses village to mean all the people who live there? | The village is a short bus ride from the town | We drove past a village with a green and a pub | *The whole village cheered when the new bridge opened | Farmers built a village near the river
exam: Which sentence uses village in the sense of the people who live there, and not the place? | A village grew slowly into a busy town over many years | Our village is smaller than the town next door | *The whole village came out to watch the summer parade | The village had a church and a small school
